<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Mecklenburg-Schwerin</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1934 CE · capital Schwerin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Republican Mecklenburg-Schwerin, which replaced one of Europe's most archaic constitutions with democracy and later an early Nazi government.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-francis-iv-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-schwerin">Grand Duke Frederick Francis IV</a> abdicated on 14 November 1918, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg-Schwerin</a> became a free state. A constitution of 1920 created a parliamentary republic, replacing the estates-based system that had survived since 1755.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The free state remained largely agricultural, with big estates and a rural labouring population, and its capital at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwerin">Schwerin</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-rostock">Rostock</a> with its university and shipyards was the main town. Politics swung between Social Democrats and nationalists, and in 1932 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazism">Nazis</a> won a majority in the Landtag elections and formed one of the first Nazi-led state governments.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1933 parliamentary rule ended and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-hildebrandt">Friedrich Hildebrandt</a> became Reich governor. On 1 January 1934 a Reich law merged it with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-mecklenburg">Free State of Mecklenburg</a>, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwerin">Schwerin</a> as capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-state-of-mecklenburg-schwerin.jpg" alt="Free State of Mecklenburg-Schwerin" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Gro%C3%9Fherzogt%C3%BCmer_Mecklenburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts